config BR2_PACKAGE_CADR_CHAOSNET
	bool "cadr-chaosnet"
	select BR2_PACKAGE_CADR_COMMON
	help
	  The Chaosnet: the program on the processing system that carries
	  packets between the CADR's Chaosnet interface in the fabric and
	  the outside world, and that answers the services the band looks
	  for.  It is the cable the interface is plugged into, and every
	  other station on that cable.

	  It serves TIME, UPTIME and STATUS always, and FILE when it is
	  given a directory to serve.  FILE is the one the machine asks
	  for first: a band that boots without it paints the window system
	  and then says its file host is not a known host.

	  Chaosnet over UDP puts the cable on the board's Ethernet, so
	  another Chaosnet host or a bridge can be a station on it.

	  It has an init script, as cadr-disk-packs and cadr-terminal do:
	  a machine that is up wants its file host to be up too, and
	  nothing is on the bus while no packet is moving.
